				</p>

				<div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
					<div class="card p-6">
						<h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-2">How the Qibla Azimuth is Calculated</h3>
						<p class="text-sm text-body leading-6">
							The Qibla is the Great-Circle forward azimuth from your current GPS coordinates to the holy Kaaba at the Masjid al-Haram in Mecca, Saudi Arabia (latitude 21° 25′ 21″ N, longitude 39° 49′ 34″ E). Using spherical trigonometry:
						</p>
						<div class="my-3 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-3 font-mono text-xs text-ink overflow-x-auto">
							<p>ΔL = λ_mecca - λ_user</p>
							<p class="mt-1">y = sin(ΔL)</p>
